\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Geometric comparison between conventional single-layer spherical embeddings and the proposed POLARIS architecture. (a) Standard spherical embeddings such as JoSE pull co-occurring synonyms and antonyms into the same hemisphere ($\cos \theta _{\text  {syn}} = 0.116$, $\cos \theta _{\text  {ant}} = 0.106$), leaving the South Pole empty. (b) POLARIS partitions $\mathbb  {S}^{p-1}$ into three functional zones: North Polar Cap ($\cos \theta \to +1$), Equatorial Belt ($\cos \theta \to 0$), and South Antipodal Pole ($\cos \theta \to -1$). (c) Three isometric spherical layers connected by $\mathcal  {O}(p)$ Householder reflections and a monotonic concentration cascade ($\kappa ^{(1)} > \kappa ^{(2)} > \kappa ^{(3)}$) separate fine-grained lexical polarity from global document topic transport.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:polaris_hook}{{1}{2}{}{}{}}
